 "summary": "Bongandanga territory (Mongala province, south of the Congo river in the Lopori basin) lies far from the eastern and Mai-Ndombe/Kwilu conflict zones and no armed group is known to hold territory in it. Bongandanga centre and the larger settlements of the Pimu, Bosondjo and Boso Mondanda health zones are policed by the Congolese National Police (PNC), with territorial and secteur administration present. Rural villages are assessed as default state (PNC) presence, with customary chiefs settling everyday disputes; security issues are banditry and local land/customary disputes. NOTE: no web research could be done for this unit (search budget exhausted, news sites blocked by the egress proxy), so this assessment rests on general background knowledge, not on 2025-2026 sources, and should be re-checked.",
